{"id": "EUVD-2026-103639", "enisaUuid": "61d68161-4366-3312-b357-492002dd3b87", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntg3: clean up PHYLIB resources on probe failure\n\ntg3_get_invariants() can register an MDIO bus and connect a PHY for\nUSE_PHYLIB devices. If tg3_init_one() later fails, its common error path\nreleases the mappings and netdev without undoing those PHYLIB resources.\n\nDisconnect the PHY and unregister the MDIO bus before the remaining\nteardown. Guard PHY cleanup with USE_PHYLIB to match tg3_phy_init(), and\ncall tg3_mdio_fini() unconditionally to match tg3_mdio_init(). The existing\nIS_CONNECTED and MDIOBUS_INITED flags make both helpers safe when\ninitialization only completed partially.\n\nThis issue was identified during our ongoing static-analysis research while\nreviewing kernel code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce86d6929d03e6b0abcb781dfa50f9f0816bff78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a449eedb3b1eb5b8b1f5ed116a1bfe85eaaf81df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0844402326d4e48a28688f93ec6442e93bb442fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e766321288b507afb70d2bfef6ba443213329f79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2abb0013b933d59ee441185df0eca9e8c0b33eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6515c41503eef849abd2c7364f34e4bb25110f90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6c0c757c65893ad7bb17e8bcf33cdd8257d7b3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a92e1a412c53dc0d9ad639e7abf8b3fc70a5b6ad"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2vwq-f5h6-r9rw", "CVE-2026-98594"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0db742ea-a209-34b1-b3a8-b63ae9f136c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "158d7abdae85e9ac43d99780c372d79c119f7626 <b6c0c757c65893ad7bb17e8bcf33cdd8257d7b3d"}, {"id": "1321b08c-9106-3f71-b4ee-bef6ed3d169f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"na